  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Omar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 3 November, 2020 Tuesday, The Third Day Of November",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. Heard Sri R.Siva Sai Swarup, learned counsel for the petitioner and the Public Prosecutor appearing on behalf of respondent-State. 3, Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the revision petition filed an application under Section 457 of Cr.P.C for grant of interim custody of his Maruti Swift Car bearing Registration No.KA 04 MG 1488 and the same was dismissed. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the said vehicle was seized on 13.12.2019 while he was carrying tobacco products and basing on the same, the crime was registered for the offences punishable under Sections 307, 353, 270, 273, 328 r/w 34 of IPC and Section 59 (1) of Food Safety And Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"FSS Act\"). He further submits except Section 307 of IPC, all other sections charged against the revision petitioner were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. In support of the same, learned counsel has placed before this Court the copies of orders in Crl.P.Nos.12 of 2020, 7799 of 2019 and 2820 of 2020. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the vehicle is very much required to the Cee eg i petitioner and retaining the same in the police station will not serve any purpose. He relied on the judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in General Insurance Council Vs. State of Andhra Pradesh!, wherein it was held thus:",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. Heard Sri R.Siva Sai Swarup, learned counsel for the petitioner and the Public Prosecutor appearing on behalf of respondent-State. 3, Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the revision petition filed an application under Section 457 of Cr.P.C for grant of interim custody of his Maruti Swift Car bearing Registration No.KA 04 MG 1488 and the same was dismissed. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the said vehicle was seized on 13.12.2019 while he was carrying tobacco products and basing on the same, the crime was registered for the offences punishable under Sections 307, 353, 270, 273, 328 r/w 34 of IPC and Section 59 (1) of Food Safety And Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"FSS Act\"). He further submits except Section 307 of IPC, all other sections charged against the revision petitioner were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. In support of the same, learned counsel has placed before this Court the copies of orders in Crl.P.Nos.12 of 2020, 7799 of 2019 and 2820 of 2020. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the vehicle is very much required to the Cee eg i petitioner and retaining the same in the police station will not serve any purpose. He relied on the judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in General Insurance Council Vs. State of Andhra Pradesh!, wherein it was held thus:",
